  "mapping": {
    "authored_date": "2026-07-18",
    "deviation_notes": "The mana-stack resource identity (RESOURCE_CONVERSION) and MoM/Indigon economy warps land cleanly, but Ball Lightning's signature 'slow-drift + 150ms tick + inverse-velocity (slower orb = more hits = more damage)' has no matching 26-geometry; approximated as a circle tick-AoE. A player would keep the mana-as-weapon feel but lose the positional skill of drifting the orb through a pack for max hits.",
    "grade": "CLOSE",
    "kit_id": "poe1-archmage",
    "mapping_json": {
      "fidelity_notes": "IDENTITY = resource-as-weapon: unreserved mana drives flat lightning damage; RESOURCE_CONVERSION is the exact T4 door (resource pool converted to weapon output). MoM (mana-as-life-buffer) and Indigon (spend-more-mana -> higher-cost -> more damage feedback loop) are the economy-warping items that land in resource_economy (cost_slope escalating captures the Indigon feedback). GEOMETRY FRICTION: Ball Lightning — a slow drifting projectile that ticks a small AoE every 150ms with inverse-velocity damage — has NO clean 26-type. Mapped as 'circle' (tick-AoE around the dwell point); the drift-and-inverse-velocity is a numeric/behavioral property the geometry enum doesn't carry. Manabond variant = line. Shock->sunder (false-friend). Delivery is subordinate to the mana-stack identity per §7.2.",
      "motion_frame": "stationary mana-caster: cast drains the pool, regen refills it, cast again — the mana bar is both cannon and shield (MoM)",
      "option_c_substrate_flags": null,
      "resource_economy": {
